#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105684 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a91e7c54-7ba7-5ea2-99a1-80510e77ac88" :knowledge-point/title "Basic Derivatives of the Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "ec8ac943-1880-5f2a-81c3-35c136126ec1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8328" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $y = 3\\tanh{x}- \\sinh{x}$." :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nFirst, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} (\\sinh x) = \\cosh x, \\quad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} (\\cosh x) = \\sinh x, \\quad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x} (\\tanh x) = \\sech^2 x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3\\tanh x - \\sinh x) \\\\\n&= 3\\frac{d}{dx}(\\tanh x) - \\frac{d}{dx}(\\sinh x) \\\\\n&= 3sech^{2} x - \\cosh x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105685 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2992a46-063e-589d-a7e9-129e9f97eee6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "3dcfc1f2-40ee-54b4-a937-0e101c7238d4" :question/math-academy-id "e-8329" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = 2x\\tanh{x}$." :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nHere, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = 2x$ and\n\n$$\nv(x)=\\tanh x\n$$\n\nSo, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= (2x)^{′} \\cdot \\tanh x + 2x \\cdot (\\tanh x)^{′} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot \\tanh x + 2x \\cdot sech^{2} x \\\\\n&= 2\\tanh x + 2xsech^{2} x \\\\\n&= 2(\\tanh x + xsech^{2} x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105686 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dbeb43f0-d94d-5ee0-b7fb-fbbe0a804cb7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Hyperbolic Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "1da70111-4e82-5fe4-b4be-08d0cc6f1110" :question/math-academy-id "e-8330" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $w(x) = \\dfrac{x^3}{\\cosh{x}}$." :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the expression for $w(x)$ is a quotient\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}\n$$\n\nwith $u(x) = x^3$ and\n\n$$\nv(x) = \\cosh{x}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nw^{′}(x) &= (u^{′}(x) \\cdot v(x) - u(x) \\cdot v^{′}(x))/([v(x)]^{2}) \\\\\n&= ((x^{3})^{′} \\cdot \\cosh x - x^{3} \\cdot (\\cosh x)^{′})/((\\cosh x)^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3x^{2} \\cdot \\cosh x - x^{3} \\cdot \\sinh x}{\\cosh^{2} x} \\\\\n&= (x^{2}(3\\cosh x - x\\sinh x))/(\\cosh^{2} x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105687 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0016464f-27c3-5f1b-a6d3-fe7b5ffb7fbd" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Hyperbolic Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "192e6748-24e3-5688-87d9-cdf379e24101" :question/math-academy-id "e-8332" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = \\cosh{\\sqrt x}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf = \\cosh g, \\qquad g = \\sqrt x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}g} \\cdot \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}g} {\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}g} = \\sinh g\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}g} {\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt x}\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{df}{dx} &= \\sinh g \\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\\n&= \\sinh \\sqrt{x} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sinh \\sqrt{x}}{2\\sqrt{x}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106536 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a91e7c54-7ba7-5ea2-99a1-80510e77ac88" :knowledge-point/title "Basic Derivatives of the Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ffe299f-7e1b-5ba3-9595-ba403dc93e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cosh x + 3\\sinh x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105365} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a7e0fe-d9c8-5a96-965e-8dae73f8db0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer